es in short time frame, further decreasing the effect of some other confounding variables on the study results.", "ctxParagraph2Feedback": null, "ctxParagraph3": "Eighty-nine patients were enrolled in the trial. Nine patients dropped out of the study, leaving only eighty patients for the final analysis. There was no significant difference among the three different groups as far as their basal characteristics were concerned. There was also no difference in the basal temperatures among all the groups. These were 38.82 (37.53-40.11)~ 38.96 (38.70-39.22)~ and 38.78 (38.63-38.93)~ in nimesulide, paracetamol' and ibuprofen-paracetamol combination groups respectively (Table 1 ).", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 1, "expertExplanation": "no information", "expertPrediction": "no information", "gptExplanation": "The study mentioned maintaining a double-blind design by preparing drugs in identical coded bottles, indicating that the allocation sequence was likely concealed until participants were enrolled and assigned to interventions.", "gptPrediction": "yes", "gptResponse": "{
