 other side-effects such as moderate virilization with oxandrolone (Stahnke et al., 1992; Job, 1993) were reported, both dependent upon the dose. When recombinant GH was tested alone, few trials documented the dose-response relation between GH and growth (Takano et al., 1992; Spoudeas et al., 1993) . The multicentre study reported here was designed to compare the effects of two randomly allocated GH doses (D1 0 : 45, D2 0 : 90 IU/kg/week) for one year in 97 girls with Turner's syndrome. After the first year of treatment, all patients treated with the lower dose were changed to 0 . 90 IU/kg/week for the 2 subsequent years.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 4, "expertExplanation": "", "expertPrediction": "qa-na", "gptExplanation": "It is likely that assessment of the outcome was influenced by knowledge of intervention received, as the study design involved comparing two randomly allocated GH doses and then switching all patients treated with the lower dose to the higher dose for the subsequent years. This knowledge could potentially bias the evaluation of the outcomes, as patients and researchers may have different expectations based on the intervention received.", "gptPrediction": "yes", "gptResponse": "{
