year of our study, G1 patients, when treated with 0 . 9 IU/kg/week (D2 dose), did not reach the height velocity of G2 patients in the first year (Table 2 ). However, over 3 years, the G1 patients who received 83 . 4% of the G2 GH dose grew only 0 . 5 cm less (mean) than G2 patients. At a mean weight of 25 kg (as for our patients at inclusion) treatment with the D1 dose for 1 out of 3 years provided a saving of around 580 IU GH per patient.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 5, "expertExplanation": "all eligible reported results for the outcome measurement correspond to all intended analyses.", "expertPrediction": "probably no", "gptExplanation": "The numerical result is likely to have been selected from multiple eligible outcome measurements within the outcome domain, as the study compares growth acceleration, height velocity, and weight outcomes over 3 years among two different GH dose groups.", "gptPrediction": "yes", "gptResponse": "{
