 estimation (NONMEM-FO) (29) (30) (31) . Levocetirizine and dextrocetirizine concentrations were determined in plasma samples by using chiral high performance liquid chromatography with tandem mass spectrometric detection. The quantification range was 12-1000 ng/ml for both validated assays. Quality control samples at 7.5, 150, and 750 ng/ml were assayed in duplicate with each batch of clinical samples (29, 30) .", "ctxParagraph2Feedback": null, "ctxParagraph3": "Cetirizine (levocetirizine) was rapidly absorbed (Fig. 2 ). Three, 12, and 18 months after cetirizine was started, the children had mean ages of 19.8, 29.0, and 35.3 months, and mean body weights of 11.9, 13.9, and 15.0 kg, and the population estimates of Cl/F were 0.77, 0.86, and 0.91 l/h, respectively. Inter-patient variability in Cl/F in the basic model was 26.1%, explained in part by the significant association between Cl/F and weight, which decreased the inter-patient variability slightly (to 24.4%) in the final model. Clearance increased linearly with weight as follows: Cl/F ¼ 0.044 l/h/kg from 0.22 l/h, the extrapolated intercept of the Cl/F vs. body weight plot.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 4, "expertExplanation": "Measurement or ascertainment of the outcome is unlikely to have differed between intervention groups as blood samples were obtained at the same time points for both cetirizine and placebo treatments, and the data collection process was standardized and documented through the use of diary cards.", "expertPrediction": "probably no", "gptExplanation": "Measurement or ascertainment of the outcome is unlikely to have differed between intervention groups as blood samples were obtained at the same time points for both cetirizine and placebo treatments, and the data collection process was standardized and documented through the use of diary cards.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{
