y basis when the child was well, and on a daily basis if the child was having symptoms of any kind. Children were examined at eight regularly scheduled visits: before treatment with cetirizine or placebo, and at 1, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, and 18 months after beginning treatment. Blood samples were obtained before, and after 3, 12, and 18 months of cetirizine treatment, when cetirizine and levocetirizine PK were presumed to be at steady-state. The time interval between blood sample collection and the previous cetirizine dose was recorded for each child. Population pharmacokinetic parameters were derived by using non-linear mixed effects modeling with first-order estimation (NONMEM-FO) (29) (30) (31) . Levocetirizine and dextrocetirizine concentrations were determined in plasma samples by using chiral high performance liquid chromatography with tandem mass spectrometric detection. The quantification range was 12-1000 ng/ml for both validated assays. Quality control samples at 7.5, 150, and 750 ng/ml were assayed in duplicate with each batch of clinical samples (29, 30) .", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 4, "expertExplanation": "There is no indication in the provided context that outcome assessors were aware of the intervention received by study participants.", "expertPrediction": "no", "gptExplanation": "There is no indication in the provided context that outcome assessors were aware of the intervention received by study participants.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{
