group, the difference between groups being statistically significant (p = 0.0001; Table 2 ). As far as GPx is concerned, a 12.9% decrease in the placebo group, and a modest increase of 10.14% in the melatonin group occurred, but the between-group difference failed to reach statistical significance (p = 0.09).", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 5, "expertExplanation": "The numerical result being assessed (30.7% increase in GRd levels in the melatonin group) is unlikely to have been selected from multiple eligible analyses of the data because the statistical significance was reported and the comparison was pre-planned between the two groups.", "expertPrediction": "no", "gptExplanation": "The numerical result being assessed (30.7% increase in GRd levels in the melatonin group) is unlikely to have been selected from multiple eligible analyses of the data because the statistical significance was reported and the comparison was pre-planned between the two groups.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{
