nd individual answer to the treatment in montelukast group only; children enrolled later, at the end of winter season (meaning at the end of heating season) responded better to treatment (Fig. 3a ). The answer to both ICS doses was independent from time of enrollment (Fig. 3b, c ).", "ctxParagraph2Feedback": null, "ctxParagraph3": "At the first visit, patients were stratified according to age (6-10 and 11-18 yr) and randomized according to a computer-generated allocation schedule for different treatment with the following: The second visit took place after 6 months of treatment. The subjectÕs ATAQ was evaluated monthly. Also, at the first and second visit, lung function testing in individual patient always took place. Compliance with asthma medication was checked; patients were asked to bring all used and unused medication to each follow-up visit.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 5, "expertExplanation": "The results were analyzed using specific statistical methods and there is no indication that multiple eligible analyses were conducted. The methods used, such as Wilcoxon test and Kruskal-Wallis test, were applied to analyze the data according to well-known statistical practices.", "expertPrediction": "no", "gptExplanation": "The results were analyzed using specific statistical methods and there is no indication that multiple eligible analyses were conducted. The methods used, such as Wilcoxon test and Kruskal-Wallis test, were applied to analyze the data according to well-known statistical practices.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{
