e was 14.3 8 1.6 years. To be eligible for inclusion, the children had to be scheduled for maxillary treatment with fixed orthodontic appliances for an expected duration of at least 6 months. Sample size was calculated on the basis of the WSL incidence reported by Øgaard et al. [2001] . With the ␣ -and ␤ -values set at 0.05 and 0.2, respectively, 132 subjects per group were needed to disclose a 20% difference between the treatment groups. After verbal and written information, the subjects as well as one of their custodians gave their consent by signing a protocol. All the children were informed on the increased risk for demineralization around their brackets and were strongly advocated to brush their teeth with 1,000-1,500 ppm fluoride toothpaste at least 2 times daily. The fluoride content in the piped drinking water was low ( ! 0.2 ppm F) in both communities.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 1, "expertExplanation": "The study had a randomized placebo-controlled double-blind design, which suggests that an allocation sequence randomization process was implemented.", "expertPrediction": "yes", "gptExplanation": "The study had a randomized placebo-controlled double-blind design, which suggests that an allocation sequence randomization process was implemented.", "gptPrediction": "yes", "gptResponse": "{
