d et al., 2001; Fornell and Twetman, 2004] . Lateral incisors were affected more often than other teeth. This may be explained by less enamel resistance due to later eruption in comparison to central incisors. Another reason may have been that the lateral incisors in many cases had a palatal position at baseline and thereby were concomitantly subjected to heavier plaque accumulation due to difficulties in cleaning. The effectiveness of the intervention was unequivocal since approximately 5 patients had to be treated in order to obtain 1 totally free from WSL development. It is also very likely that the efficiency of the treatment outcome was favourable from an economic point of view since no extra recalls with administrative costs were needed. Patients undergoing orthodontic treatment with fixed appliances are often seen for adjustments with 6-to 8-week intervals. The extra time needed for varnish application around the brackets was relatively short. It should be stressed that no side-or adverse effects were reported during the course of the study and that the topical treatment with the uncoloured varnish had a high acceptance among the subjects. The dropout patients aborted their orthodontic treatment for other reasons. The present finding that the baseline caries experience (DMFS) did not correlate to the WSL incidence was somewhat unexpected in the light of previous findings. In a study by Fornell and Twetman [2004] it was shown that the presence of initial proximal lesions on bite-wing radiographs at the time of insertion of fixed appliances was a relatively strong predictor for WSL development during the treatment period. In the present study the overall caries prevalence was low and more than one third of participants were caries-free at baseline. It should also be pinpointed that the DMFS values mostly reflected accumulated caries experience and mainly included occlusal fillings in first permanent molars. It is possible that initial proximal caries may have had a better correlation to caries risk in this age group.", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 3, "expertExplanation": "There is no indication in the text that missingness in the outcome depended on its true value. The reasons for dropping out of the study were due to relocation or violation of the treatment protocol, and technical failure with the photos, which are unlikely to be related to the true value of the outcome.", "expertPrediction": "no", "gptExplanation": "There is no indication in the text that missingness in the outcome depended on its true value. The reasons for dropping out of the study were due to relocation or violation of the treatment protocol, and technical failure with the photos, which are unlikely to be related to the true value of the outcome.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{ 
