multiple eligible outcome measurements (e.g. scales, definitions, time points) within the outcome domain?"}, {"addedParagraph1": null, "addedParagraph1Feedback": null, "addedParagraph1Score": null, "addedParagraph2": null, "addedParagraph2Feedback": null, "addedParagraph2Score": null, "addedParagraph3": null, "addedParagraph3Feedback": null, "addedParagraph3Score": null, "ctxP1Score": "0.294", "ctxP2Score": "0.292", "ctxP3Score": "0.273", "ctxParagraph1": "All data were processed using SPSS software (version 14.0) and the colour code was not broken until the calculations had been performed. The categorized scores were compared by chi-square tests and the differences between the groups were assessed by the unpaired Wilcoxon test. The progression score was constructed by subtracting the debond score from that registered at baseline. The level of significance was set to 5% (p ! 0.05). The effectiveness of the intervention was calculated and expressed as the absolute risk reduction (ARR, expressed as percent) and number needed to treat (1/ARR).", "ctxParagraph1Feedback": null, "ctxParagraph2": "The study was carried out in a double-blind fashion with a randomized placebo-controlled design with two parallel arms. The two-centre project was approved by the local Ethics Committee of Umeå University. The patients were assigned to one of the two groups on the basis of odd and even numbers from a dice. The subjects were treated by topical applications of either the active or the placebo varnish immediately after bonding the brackets and then in connection with every scheduled follow-up during the period of fixed appliances or approximately every 6th week. The primary outcome measure was incidence or progression of WSL as registered with a four-step score as described below.", "ctxParagraph2Feedback": null, "ctxParagraph3": "The results were clear-cut and the null hypothesis could firmly be rejected. The findings are supportive of and reinforcing the findings from previous studies in vivo [Øgaard et al., 2001; Vivaldi-Rodrigues et al., 2006] .", "ctxParagraph3Feedback": null, "domain_number": 5, "expertExplanation": "The text states that the categorized scores were compared by chi-square tests and the differences between the groups were assessed by the unpaired Wilcoxon test. It also states that the level of significance was set to 5% (p ! 0.05). The results of these analysis were reported in accordance to this analysis plan.", "expertPrediction": "probably no", "gptExplanation": "The text states that the categorized scores were compared by chi-square tests and the differences between the groups were assessed by the unpaired Wilcoxon test. It also states that the level of significance was set to 5% (p ! 0.05). Therefore, it seems that the numerical result being assessed was not selected from multiple eligible analyses of the data.", "gptPrediction": "no", "gptResponse": "{
